# Python Day 03 — Comments, Data Types & Collections

## 1. Comments

Comments are ignored by the Python interpreter and are used to explain code, improve readability, add notes, or temporarily disable code.

### Single-Line Comment

Uses `#`

```python
# This is a comment
print("Hello")
```

### Multi-Line Text / Documentation

Python has no special multi-line comment syntax. Triple quotes are commonly used for multi-line text or **docstrings**.

```python
"""
This is multi-line text.
"""
```

> Triple-quoted text is technically a string literal; when placed inside a module, function, or class for documentation, it becomes a docstring.

---

## 2. Swapping Variables

Swapping means exchanging two variable values.

### Method 1 — Third Variable

```python
temp = a
a = b
b = temp
```

### Method 2 — Arithmetic

```python
a = a + b
b = a - b
a = a - b
```

### Method 3 — Pythonic Way ⭐ Recommended

```python
a, b = b, a
```

Example:

```python
a = 10
b = 20
a, b = b, a
print(a, b)
# 20 10
```

## The Pythonic method is the recommended approach.

## 3. Variables

A variable is a **name that refers to an object/value**.

```python
age = 22
name = "Harish"
percentage = 95.5
```

Python automatically determines the data type from the assigned value.

